   418:     #  anchor rule's principle one level down -- a row varying two bits cannot say which fired.  The ruling:
   419:     #  the anchor rule repairs an oracle that compares a path with ITSELF, which is not the situation here,
   420:     #  since the joint row already checks concrete vector and register expectations; and the carrier bounds row
   421:     #  demand "per enumerated mutant, never per attribution need".  Removing this row loses NONE of the 56
